The number of bags of holding doesn't help you w.r.t. your burden.  It
will weigh the same.  The BUC status matters.  People may have
personal-playing-style reasons to have more than one bag, the most
obvious is to split up stuff in case something happens to your primary.
 Let's not go there.

Gold is much less important once you have maxed out protection.  You
can pay the Oracle for words of wisdom.  You can just buy stuff from
the stores instead of bothering with theft or merchanticide.

Inventory mgmt is the game once you get lots of stuff.  You have to
stash your stuff.  Perhaps we just met; the last level I did (last
night) was a bones file from Hearse in which the PC Elbereth'ed a
square in the middle of the level and dropped a BoH on it.  The BoH was
uncursed, but it was *so*loaded*down* with crap (about 2 alphabets
worth including ~12 spellbooks) that I couldn't get it up the stairs to
my stash to sort even after I blessed it.  (The former owner didn't
leave a grave; he either choked on food, or he bumped into a floating
eye and then got killed by a gargoyle or a lizard.  He was survived a
hungry but very nice warhorse.)

Once you get to a higher level and down deep, some of it has to be worn
all the time, some in open inventory, some can be in a bag, and some
you can leave behind.  I know I'm not being very specific, so I'll be
specific.

Stash:
Spellbooks! (weigh a lot)
Backup armor except cloaks
Backup tools
Backup weapons except daggers
unlabelled scrolls (esp if you don't have a marker)
uncursed water and potions that aren't useful in battle
some food
duplicates of most rings
gems except a few hard gems
Any other junk that is valuable but the RNG seems to be particularly
generous with today

Keep in bag:
Food
Backup cloak
Most wands (NOT CANCELLATION!!)
Pickaxe! (if you aren't using it as a weapon) weighs a ton
other tools if not in use
Most scrolls
zorkmids
a few gems including one hard one


Open inventory:
Daggers/ammo
rings/amulets you may want in melee
one or a few wands you may want in melee
one or a few scrolls you may want in melee
1 holy water
lizard corpse
luckstone
blindfold/towel
tools in active use
a small amount of gold

Wear/wield:
Primary armor
Primary weapon
(optional, level dependent) reflection, searching, warning, ESP,
protection,...

The last item is very dependent on personal playing style.

Also note that armor weighs a lot.  There is a philosophy that says
there are 4 kinds of armor suits:  [studded] leather, mithril, dragon
scale mail, and stuff you don't want.  This is also dependent on
personal playing style; my current game I found a blessed enchanted
crystal plate mail, and I'm dealing with it for now.



